       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered:** ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily, which is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Maximum:** the labeled limit for adults is 3,200 mg/day, and that is the ceiling for supervised use. Most regimens stay at or below 2,400 mg/day. A single dose is usually capped at 800 mg.\n- **Risk:** this is twice the maximum daily dose. It carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n1600 mg may be the intended total daily dose, or the order may have a decimal or frequency error. Here are some common regimens:\n\n- 400 mg by mouth four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- 600 mg by mouth three times daily (1,800 mg/day)\n- 800 mg by mouth three times daily (2,400 mg/day), which is the usual maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing\n\nTell me which regimen you want, or confirm that you really mean 1600 mg four times daily. If you confirm it, I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first. I can add a note to the order with the indication and the intended duration."
      }
